From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:57:08 -0700
Subject: Prevent dirty slot assignments during layout and frame rect updates

FlatTreeTraversal::TraverseParent calls Node::AssignedSlot, which
triggers SlotAssignment::RecalcAssignment if a shadow root still has
NeedsSlotAssignmentRecalc() set. During RecalcAssignment,
HTMLSlotElement::DetachDisplayLockedAssignedNodesLayoutTreeIfNeeded
synchronously detaches the layout tree of display-locked assigned
nodes. If a shadow root remains dirty into layout (e.g.
BlockNode::AttachScrollMarkers) or frame rect propagation
(LocalFrameView::PropagateFrameRectsRecursively), detaching the layout
tree mutates vectors being iterated on the stack, such as
ColumnPseudoElementsVector or LocalFrameView::plugins_.

A slottable Node stores two slot pointers on FlatTreeNodeData:
assigned_slot_ (the <slot> it is currently slotted into in the flat
tree as a direct child of that slot's host) and manually_assigned_slot_
(the candidate <slot> imperatively assigned via
HTMLSlotElement.prototype.assign(), which the DOM spec requires
preserving even while the node is outside the shadow host). However,
Blink also uses SlotAssignmentMode::kManual internally for User-Agent
shadow roots on <details>, <select>, and <optgroup>, which run
Element::ManuallyAssignSlots() during
SlotAssignment::RecalcAssignment() and call ua_slot->Assign() on their
current children.

Shadow roots could remain dirty past
SlotAssignmentEngine::RecalcSlotAssignments() for two reasons:

1. HTMLSlotElement::Assign() treated UA slots identically to author
   slots and shared Node::ManuallyAssignedSlot() for both. When a node
   previously passed to an author slot's assign() was moved into a
   <details> element, <details>'s UA slot assignment ran
   ManuallyAssignSlots() -> content_slot_->Assign() inside
   RecalcAssignment(), saw previous_slot = node->ManuallyAssignedSlot()
   pointing to the author <slot>, erased the node from the author
   slot's manually_assigned_nodes_, overwrote
   node->SetManuallyAssignedSlot(content_slot_), and called
   DidSlotChange() -> SetNeedsAssignmentRecalc() on the author shadow
   root mid-recalc. Because
   SlotAssignmentEngine::RecalcSlotAssignments() performs a single pass
   over a snapshot of shadow_roots_needing_recalc_, the newly dirtied
   author shadow root remained dirty after RecalcSlotAssignments()
   returned. Sharing Node::ManuallyAssignedSlot() also violated the DOM
   spec by destroying the node's author slot.assign() association when
   moved into <details> (and conversely allowed
   author_slot.assign(details_child) to steal a child from <details>'s
   UA slot).

2. SlotAssignment::DidRemoveSlot() for manual slotting cleared
   candidate nodes without calling SetNeedsAssignmentRecalc().

This patch fixes these issues by construction:

- In HTMLSlotElement::Assign(), only read or modify
  Node::ManuallyAssignedSlot() and previous_slot when
  !IsInUserAgentShadowRoot(). UA slots only update their own
  manually_assigned_nodes_ set without touching
  Node::ManuallyAssignedSlot() or dirtying author shadow roots. In
  SlotAssignment::FindSlotInManualSlotting(), check the UA slots'
  ManuallyAssignedNodes() when owner_->IsUserAgent() is true.
- Call SetNeedsAssignmentRecalc() in SlotAssignment::DidRemoveSlot()
  when a removed manual slot had candidate assigned nodes.
- Add SlotAssignmentRecalcForbiddenScope in
  LocalFrameView::PerformLayout() and
  LocalFrameView::PropagateFrameRectsRecursively() to enforce via
  DCHECK that slot assignment recalculation is never triggered in those
  phases.

